## Lore

Quill Men are the smallest and quickest of the Haven Mutants: slender, human
below the neck, with a long rat-like snout and a mane of stiff M.D.C. spines
where hair should be. The spines run from the brow down to the middle of the
back, armour the rear of the body, soften a fall, and can be pulled out and
used as blades or tools. Their skin is mottled and freckled, and most paint
patterns around their eyes and along their arms.

They care little for complex machinery and rarely bother with armor, but they
adore firearms and anything small and fast. Beast Men build them gyro-balanced
motor unicycles, and Quill Men race these over rubble heaps and through gullies
with reckless skill. Heights, speed and falls hold no terror for them.

They are Madhaven''s raiders and pranksters. Outsiders are their favourite
marks, though Mantis Men, Leopard Men, Savage Lummox and the Garden folk
get harassed too. At play they behave like unruly kids, whooping and
daring each other; on a raid they burst out of a dust cloud with guns firing.
Unlike some clans, they would rather frighten intruders off than kill, eat or
enslave them. They will kill when they must and will happily loot or wreck a
camp, but they are not murderers.

## Mutant Shaman

Any sizable clan is led by a Shaman, who keeps the race''s attributes and
abilities and gains the bonuses the `shaman` variant carries: +2 I.Q., +1D4+2
M.A., +3D6+10 P.P.E. at the start and 1D6 more P.P.E. per level.

The Shaman''s skills (Animal Husbandry, Literacy in American, Medicinal
Brewing, Dance, Fasting, both Histories, Holistic Medicine, Public Speaking,
Sing and Veterinary Science) are added by the variant. **In the book they
REPLACE every Secondary skill, every Piloting skill and every modern W.P.** A
Shaman never uses a modern weapon, vehicle or machine. The app cannot remove
skills through a variant, so the player and G.M. drop those picks by hand.

A Shaman advances on the **Gateway Knight & Mutant Shaman** ladder (printed
79), not the Haven Mutant one: 0, 2,351, 4,701, 9,401, 18,801, 28,001, 38,001,
53,001, 77,001, 102,001, 143,001, 195,201, 240,401, 310,601, 360,801.

Shamans are also the clan''s lawgivers, judges and chiefs, and they can pray to
Isis, the Mighty Lady:

- **Prayer of Strength**: 01-20%, +5% per level, to be heard. Grants +6 P.S.,
  +1D4x10 M.D.C., and 48 hours without food or water with no ill effect. Up to
  six times a year.
- **Prayer of Inspiration or Wisdom**: 01-12%, +3% per level (+10% after a
  week of fasting). If Isis hears, a dream brings insight, an idea or a warning
  about the matter prayed on.

## Starting Equipment

A motorized unicycle with 2D6+88 M.D.C. (top speed 160 mph, handles gravel and
rough ground, can lean 45 degrees and jump 10 feet; riders are such small,
low, moving targets that attackers lose their usual strike bonuses and even an
aimed Called Shot is only +1). Power: 15% gasoline (10 gallons, 300 miles),
20% electric (200 miles), 45% E-Clips (180 miles), 20% nuclear (15 years).
Anyone else riding one needs the Motorcycle skill and is -20%, plus -10% per
10 mph above 40 mph.

Also a Mutant Bone Sickle and a Bone Dagger, a radio communicator, 1D4 markers,
1D4 pieces of chalk, 1D4+1 cans of spray paint, one weapon per W.P. with 1D4+2
extra clips each, 1D6 days of food and water, optional patchwork light armor
of 4D6+6 M.D.C. (seldom worn), pants, boots, leather gloves and wristband, a
utility belt, a satchel, a bike saddlebag, 1D4 medium sacks, a waterskin,
binoculars, a passive nightvision scope for one gun, 30 feet of rope, a bone
cross, goggles, sunglasses, an air filter and personal items.

## GM Notes

Alignments run mostly Anarchist (50%), Unprincipled (25%) or Miscreant (10%).
Size 5 to 5.5 feet, 100 to 140 lbs. They could live to 80, but reckless living
brings the average down to 1D6+34 years; females live 1D10 years longer. NPCs
average level 1D4+2.

Like other mutants they stick to their own clan but deal amicably with other
mutants. Unusually, Quill Men find the White Rose Knights friendly and would
be first to help them. They trade with other mutants, the Garden, Horune Pirates,
bandits, adventurers and Jersey Side barbarians, trusting no outsider. They
have no love for slavers, barbarians, Horune Pirates or Splugorth''s Minions but
trade with them anyway; their foes are intruders, madmen, ghosts, monsters,
Undead Horrors and magical creatures. They live at or near ground level, favour
tunnels, sewers and caves, and mark their turf and roads with spray-paint
graffiti.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'quill-men');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'quill-men';

